# SecurePharma — Documentation Rules

> Always apply. Companion to `structure.mdc`. Together they keep the repo tidy.

## 1. The single rule of thumb

> **Markdown documentation belongs in `docs/`. Only `README.md` lives at the repo root.**

If you (the agent) are about to create a new `.md` file anywhere in the repo, STOP and apply the table in Section 2 of `structure.mdc` first.

## 2. Folder map for documentation

```
docs/
├── README.md              # Index / table of contents of docs/
├── INSTALL.md             # How to install + run locally
├── FEATURES.md            # Functional analysis (from the project brief)
├── IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md # Living implementation plan (all phases)
├── <topic>.md             # Other living docs (SECURITY.md, TESTING.md, ADR-…, …)
└── archive/               # Frozen/completed/obsolete docs
    └── <PHASE>_<NAME>.md  # E.g. PHASE1_CHECKLIST.md after phase done
```

## 3. Naming conventions

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Living doc | `UPPER_SNAKE.md` or `Title-Case.md` | `INSTALL.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `api-design.md` |
| Phase checklist (done) | `PHASE<n>_<TOPIC>.md` | `PHASE1_CHECKLIST.md` |
| ADR | `ADR-NNN-short-slug.md` | `ADR-001-use-mssql.md` |
| Archived doc | Same as original, just placed in `archive/` |

## 4. README.md (root) contract

`./README.md` is the **only** `.md` at repo root. It must:
- Be ≤ ~200 lines. Long content → link to `docs/`.
- Link out (using repo-relative paths) to every living doc under `docs/`.
- Stay in sync: if you add a new file under `docs/`, add its row to the "Tài liệu" table in `README.md`.
- Never duplicate content that already lives in `docs/`.

## 5. docs/README.md (index) contract

`docs/README.md` is OPTIONAL but recommended when there are ≥3 docs. It should:
- Be a short table of contents linking to every sibling file (and to `archive/`).
- Group docs by topic if helpful (e.g. "Setup", "Phases", "Archive").

## 6. Internal links — keep them valid

When you move or rename any `.md` file:
1. Grep the whole repo (excluding `node_modules/`) for the old filename.
2. Update every link found — in other `.md` files AND in code comments that mention the doc.
3. Re-run the grep to confirm no dangling references remain.

Always use **repo-relative paths** in markdown links (`./docs/INSTALL.md` from root, `../INSTALL.md` from `docs/archive/`). Never use absolute filesystem paths.

## 7. Writing style (Vietnamese project)

- The project docs are currently in Vietnamese. Match the existing tone: short, structured, lots of tables and checkboxes.
- One H1 per file (the title). Use H2 / H3 for sections.
- Use emoji sparingly in headings (the codebase uses 🏥 🔐 🚀 ✅ — keep that style if matching an existing doc).
- Code paths inside backticks: `` `backend/src/app.js` ``.
- Commands inside fenced blocks with the language tag: ` ```bash `.

## 8. When the user asks to "create docs / write documentation"

Default workflow:
1. Propose the path under `docs/` (not root) before writing.
2. If the doc is for a phase already marked ✅ in the plan → suggest putting it in `docs/archive/` instead.
3. Create the file.
4. If a root `README.md` exists, add/update the corresponding link row.
5. Confirm with the user before creating multiple docs in one go.

## 9. Anti-patterns to flag and refuse

- Creating `*.md` at repo root other than `README.md`.
- Creating a new `CHECKLIST.md` at root for an already-completed phase (use `docs/archive/`).
- Duplicating content that already exists in another doc — link to it instead.
- Absolute or `file:///` paths in markdown links.
- Dead links to docs that have been moved or renamed.
